---
code: K0021
title: Duplicate Else
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, control-flow, if, else]
description: "'else' clause has no matching 'if' or duplicates an existing 'else'"
---

An `else` keyword appeared without a preceding `if` expression, or an `if ... else` expression already has an `else` branch. Each `if` expression accepts at most one `else` clause (or chained `else if ... else`).

## Example

This error occurs when a stray `else` appears on its own or when a second `else` is attached to an `if` expression:

```kura
fn label(flag: Bool): String =>
  if flag {
    "yes"
  } else {
    "no"
  } else {
    "maybe"
  }
```

## Solution

Remove the extra `else` branch, or chain additional conditions using `else if`:

```kura
fn label(flag: Bool, other: Bool): String =>
  if flag {
    "yes"
  } else if other {
    "maybe"
  } else {
    "no"
  }
```
